ough fsmMutateCh; FSM.Apply has an interface promise that entries are committed by a majority. This identifies a question about a bounded matching request followed by a divergent local suffix, not yet an executed violation.\",\n        \"remaining\": [\n          \"Complete the core backbone through startup/snapshot recovery, membership transition rules, asynchronous replication ownership, heartbeat dispatch and FSM completion before marking the overview usable.\",\n          \"Determine whether an actual permitted leader/follower history can supply a bounded AppendEntries batch ending before a divergent local suffix while LeaderCommitIndex extends into that suffix; inspect batching, transport ordering, previous-prefix backtracking and alternative truncation protection.\",\n          \"Establish the precise majority-commit obligation and same-history identity of any local suffix command before constructing a formal comparison. A source-level numerical bound alone is not a violating witness.\"\n        ],\n        \"understanding\": \"updated\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The sourced producer and consumer use different prefix bounds. Term checks and conflict truncation protect supplied entries; whether they also protect an unsupplied suffix depends on reachable history and request construction. No target was executed, no map readiness is claimed, and no conclusion is drawn from generic Raft expectations.\",\n        \"question_updates\": {}\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pending_work\": [],\n  \"current\": {\n    \"phase\": \"executed\",\n    \"operation_id\": \"174633b57ee34ae9b576f378b2405458\",\n    \"action\": \"research\"\n  },\n  \"latest_decision\": {\n    \"operation_id\": \"174633b57ee34ae9b576f378b2405458\",\n    \"action\": \"research\",\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"selections\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"operation_id\": \"174633b57ee34ae9b576f378b2405458\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"stop\": {},\n  \"stop_rea